+Light travels fast and doesn't stay very long in nanophotonic devices due to propagation losses. My work uses extreme dispersion, engineered with coherent atoms doped into the material, to slow it down dramatically. In resonators, one striking outcome of this is a record-high increase in cavity lifetime.
+
+I'm also exploring novel electro-optic effects, using electro-optic modulation to couple slow-light or polaritonic modes, and collaborating with Prof. Hafezi's group on topological photonics in thin-film lithium niobate (TFLN), using multiple timescales to relax phase matching and enable poling-free nonlinear effects.
